      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Hereditary deficiency of C1-esterase inhibitor (C1-INH) which clinically manifests as hereditary angioedema is a rare disorder. In previously not diagnosed cases, a fatality rate of up to 30 % has been reported. The diagnosis of C1-esterase inhibitor deficiency should not be missed in patients presenting with angioedema in the face, stem or extremities. We report the case of a 17-year-old girl with recurrent abdominal pain and swelling of the hands."},
